Release: **@RELEASE@**
Source commit: `@SOURCE_COMMIT@`

## Highlights

- Browser-login callbacks are now supervised. The short-lived helper is bound to
  30 seconds and cleaned up as a process group if Unity/Wine fails to exit, so it
  cannot leave a second black window behind. The running game is never signalled.
- Landscape protection. The launcher requests a 1280×720 window and keeps
  landscape tiles tiled; owned portrait game/callback windows float for the
  session because the Windows client does not ship its portrait menu/match scenes.
- Launcher internals moved into focused configuration, download, process,
  verification, CLI, and desktop packages. The CLI, JSON schemas, state files,
  installer verification, locking, desktop integration, and privacy behavior are
  unchanged.
- The v0.5.0 maintenance experience remains available: live local status, the
  compact companion with status schema 1, measured download progress, recoverable
  interrupted setup, confirmed recovery actions, and privacy-safe support reports.

## Validation and known limits

The candidate passed ready/idle preflight and all 15 doctor checks. A live run
confirmed a fresh browser logout/login, a helper window that closed by itself
within about 3.5 seconds, menu/match transitions, one completed online match, and
a normal Play exit with the original callback handler restored and no session
lock, cleanup guard, marker, game window, or owned game process left behind. See
the [validation record](https://github.com/hucKOder/omarchy-ptcgl/blob/@SOURCE_COMMIT@/docs/VALIDATION.md).

The live helper exited before its deadline, so the timeout kill itself is covered
by a real-process regression test with a TERM-ignoring helper rather than by the
live run. This is a lifecycle mitigation for the observed Unity/Wine shutdown
hang, not a native root-cause fix. Window correction is reactive: arbitrary
portrait scene transitions and atomic correction during intentional portrait
resizes remain unsupported.

Real repair/interrupted-install recovery, vertical-bar layout, and clean-OS
provisioning remain unverified follow-ups accepted by the maintainer for this
release. Automated fixture coverage is not a claim that those real-machine checks
passed. Companion marketplace submission remains separate.

The default bootstrap and companion's install/upgrade button select this stable
release. Launcher v0.5.0 or later supplies the status schema required by the
companion; its install/upgrade action no longer needs a prerelease pin. Close the
game before installing or upgrading. Existing prefix and selected Proton runtime
are retained.

## Install

Copy this one line into your terminal as your regular desktop user:

```bash
bash -c 'script=$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hucKOder/omarchy-ptcgl/@SOURCE_COMMIT@/bootstrap.sh) && bash -c "$script" -- --release @RELEASE@ --source-commit @SOURCE_COMMIT@'
```

The source bootstrap is trusted from GitHub over HTTPS; it installs verification
tools from system repositories, then authenticates the release installer and
launcher before executing them. No AUR packages or GitHub login are needed.

### Manual, independently pinned installation

Requires x86-64 Omarchy, its Lua Hyprland configuration (Hyprland 0.55+),
working XWayland/Vulkan, and roughly 8 GB of free space. Close the game before
installing or upgrading the launcher.

1. Install the bootstrap tools with `omarchy pkg add github-cli curl jq coreutils ca-certificates`.
   GitHub CLI 2.102.0 is tested; the block below checks the required verification
   capabilities. No GitHub login is required for bundle-based verification.
2. Copy the **entire block** below into Bash as your regular desktop user. The
   release and source commit are already selected. This block verifies the
   downloaded installer **before executing it**, then installs the launcher and
   game. There is no second installer command to run afterward.

```bash
(
  set -euo pipefail
  release='@RELEASE@'
  source_commit='@SOURCE_COMMIT@'
  repository='hucKOder/omarchy-ptcgl'
  fail() { printf 'Error: %s\n' "$*" >&2; exit 1; }
  (( EUID != 0 )) || fail 'Run as your desktop user, without sudo.'
  [[ $(uname -s) == Linux && $(uname -m) == x86_64 ]] || fail 'x86-64 Linux is required.'
  command -v omarchy >/dev/null || fail 'Run this on Omarchy.'
  [[ -z ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-} || $XDG_CONFIG_HOME == /* ]] || fail 'XDG_CONFIG_HOME must be an absolute path.'
  [[ -f ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/hypr/hyprland.lua ]] || fail 'Omarchy Lua Hyprland configuration is required (Hyprland 0.55+).'
  for tool in curl jq gh sha256sum; do
    command -v "$tool" >/dev/null || fail "Missing $tool. Run: omarchy pkg add github-cli curl jq coreutils"
  done
  verify_help=$(gh attestation verify --help) || fail 'Update github-cli to a version supporting artifact attestations.'
  for option in --bundle --hostname --repo --cert-identity --cert-oidc-issuer --source-ref --source-digest --signer-digest --deny-self-hosted-runners --predicate-type; do
    [[ $verify_help == *"$option"* ]] || fail "GitHub CLI is missing $option. Update github-cli through Omarchy, then retry this block."
  done
  work_dir=$(mktemp -d)
  trap 'rm -rf -- "$work_dir"' EXIT
  base="https://github.com/$repository/releases/download/$release"
  printf 'Verifying installer for %s\nSource commit: %s\n' "$release" "$source_commit"
  for asset in install.sh release.sigstore.json; do
    curl --proto '=https' --proto-redir '=https' -fsSL --retry 3 \
      "$base/$asset" --output "$work_dir/$asset" || fail 'Download failed. Retry this block; installation has not started.'
  done
  gh attestation verify "$work_dir/install.sh" \
    --bundle "$work_dir/release.sigstore.json" --hostname github.com \
    --repo "$repository" \
    --cert-identity "https://github.com/$repository/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/tags/$release" \
    --cert-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com \
    --source-ref "refs/tags/$release" --source-digest "$source_commit" \
    --signer-digest "$source_commit" --deny-self-hosted-runners \
    --predicate-type https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1 || fail 'Installer authentication failed; installation has not started.'
  bash "$work_dir/install.sh" --release "$release" --source-commit "$source_commit"
)
```

Omarchy requests your sudo password for system packages. Proton and the official
game are downloaded during setup. When **Installed!** appears, open **Pokémon TCG
Live (Omarchy)** from the app menu and sign in through your browser.

MSI signature, publisher, and certificate-chain verification is built into the
launcher. No AUR packages or separate signature-verification tool are required.

### Launcher-only installation or upgrade

Add `--launcher-only` to the final `bash` command in the block above. It uses the
same verified release while leaving game setup for the first launch and retaining
the existing game prefix and selected Proton profile.

### If setup fails

- Before launcher installation: fix the reported prerequisite or verification
  problem and retry the block.
- After launcher installation, interrupted downloads/setup: run
  `ptcgl-omarchy setup` to retry.
- If Windows Installer failed or was interrupted: close the game and run
  `ptcgl-omarchy repair`.

For diagnostics, use `ptcgl-omarchy doctor`. See
[the update and recovery guide](https://github.com/hucKOder/omarchy-ptcgl/blob/@SOURCE_COMMIT@/docs/UPDATES.md)
for details.
